Alright Denis, let's outline a Remotion and Next.js app! Here's a basic structure to get you started:

```jsx
// pages/index.tsx
import React from 'react';
import { Video, useRemotionRoot } from '@remotion/react';
import { getVideoProps } from '@remotion/server/dist/render';
import { getFonts } from './fonts';

export const Root = () => {
  const { height, width, ...rootProps } = useRemotionRoot();
  return (
    <div {...rootProps} style={{ height, width }}>
      <Video {...getVideoProps()} />
      <Content />
    </div>
  );
};

const Content = () => {
  return (
    <div>
      {/* Your app content goes here */}
    </div>
  );
};

export async function getStaticProps() {
  return {
    props: {
      fonts: getFonts(),
    },
  };
}
```

This sets up a basic Remotion app with Next.js static site generation. You can now add your video content and other components within the `Content` component. Remember to install and configure the necessary dependencies for Remotion and Next.js.

For the `fonts.ts` file:

```ts
// fonts.ts
import { loadFont } from '@remotion/font-loader';

export const getFonts = async () => {
  await loadFont({ family: 'Arial', source: { url: '/fonts/Arial.ttf' } });
  // Load other fonts here...
};
```

And don't forget to include the necessary font files in your project.

This should give you a good starting point for your Remotion and Next.js app. Let me know if you need any further assistance or have additional requirements!

